WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:10.790
Hi, welcome back to the lam rim (LAM RIM), and we're on episode three.

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:16.510
We're calling this episode the same name as the whole lam rim, which is

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:20.389
Love in the Time of the Virus--or did we say "Times?"

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:25.400
Love in the Time of the Virus.

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:29.660
We're going to start here in the Tibetan.

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:34.120
chang shar sanggye wangchuk gyelpoy shing na--
(BYANG SHAR SANGS RGYAS DBANG PHYUG RGYAL PO'I ZHING NA)

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:37.800
This means a paradise

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:40.500
and the word for paradise

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:44.180
in Sanskrit is kshetra (kṣetra), and in Tibetan it's shing (ZHING).

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:49.340
It means a beautiful place

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:51.520
where everything is perfect.

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:54.440
I imagine they're playing rock &amp; roll there all day long.

00:00:54.880 --> 00:01:00.940
There's a special one that's supposed to be located chang shar (BYANG SHAR), means

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:03.080
in the northeast of the universe.

00:01:03.366 --> 00:01:05.440
So nobody knows where that is exactly,

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:09.399
but there's a tradition to say it's in the northeast.

00:01:09.399 --> 00:01:13.669
Amitabha's paradise, for example, is said to be in the western direction.

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:15.940
So in the northeast,

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:19.020
there's supposed to be a Buddha paradise,

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:22.420
and the Buddha who's the boss there 

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:24.396
is called Wangchuk Gyalpo (DBANG PHYUG RGYAL PO),

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:30.180
which means the "king of kings" or the "king of all the extremely powerful beings."

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:36.820
In that Buddha paradise,

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:39.160
everything's going well--

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:43.340
it's like everything is good. There's no problems. Everything is nice.

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:45.260
It's especially nice,

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:50.440
like it's supposed to be one of the five-star Buddha paradises.

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:58.280
They say people there, of course, they treat other people nice.

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:00.960
They're nice to other people.

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:04.360
So they are what we call morality,

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:06.740
they are keeping it--tsultrim (TSUL KHRIMS).

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:10.600
They are keeping it well, they are treating other people sweetly.

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:16.540
If you sit in that Buddha paradise and you treat other people really nice,

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:19.666
for millions and millions of years--

00:02:19.666 --> 00:02:21.200
kelpay bar sungba le
(BSKAL PA'I BAR BSRUNG BA LAS)

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:23.378
Compared to that,

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:25.980
if you come to mi je jikten (MI MJED 'JIG RTEN)...

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:29.940
and this is a very unusual word, mi je jikten.  

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:31.240
It's very confusing--

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:35.040
it has confused many people in history,

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:38.380
but it's a word for our world

00:02:39.020 --> 00:02:41.640
which is called Jambudvīpa,

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:45.560
the dzam bu ('DZAM BU) continent is our world.

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:48.740
So it just means here, on our planet.

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:51.700
mi je (MI MJED) means "not afraid"

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:54.380
and jikten gyi kham ('JIG RTEN GYI KHAMS) means "loka," it means "world."

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:57.840
People ask in the ancient books:

00:02:58.140 --> 00:03:02.380
why is the world where people are not afraid...

00:03:02.380 --> 00:03:05.860
why is that a nickname for this planet Earth? 

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:09.400
The traditional explanation of this word

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:13.900
is that people here are not afraid to study the Dharma.

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:20.820
We have a really good mix of stability and chaos in our world.

00:03:20.980 --> 00:03:24.820
So people are... they're happy to study the Dharma.

00:03:24.820 --> 00:03:26.580
They're not afraid--mi je.

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:29.380
They're not afraid to study the Dharma.

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:32.660
jikten gyi kham su tunpa shakya tuppay tenpa dir
('JIG RTEN GYI KHAMS SU STON PA SH'AKYA THUB PA'I BSTAN PA 'DIR)

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:35.058
Here in the teachings, you know,

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:39.440
the teaching world of Shakyamuni,

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:43.040
our Buddha. I like to call him our Buddha.

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:45.720
tsultrim nyin chik la sungwa
(TSUL KHRIMS NYIN GCIG LA BSRUNG BA)

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:50.380
If you keep... if you're nice to other people in this crazy, mixed-up world

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:53.120
for just one day,

00:03:53.660 --> 00:03:55.880
then it's better seeds,

00:03:56.080 --> 00:04:03.320
it's more powerful seeds, than sitting in that five-star Buddha paradise and being nice to other people.

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:04.660
Why?

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:11.620
Because this world is a place with a mixture of goodness and chaos.

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:14.300
Especially we're seeing it now

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:17.660
in the times of the virus--the virus is spreading.

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:23.620
And you can feel people are on edge--people nowadays, they're on edge.

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:27.400
Things... it feels like things can happen suddenly.

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:34.040
People have been... I don't know, people in America, we were locked up.

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:38.260
We've never been locked up and we don't like to be locked up. 

00:04:39.180 --> 00:04:41.129
Actually people don't like to listen, to be told what to do.

00:04:41.129 --> 00:04:48.319
Then we were told to stay in our houses and you could feel

00:04:48.860 --> 00:04:52.340
the tension growing in this big country,

00:04:52.340 --> 00:04:56.640
in this whole country. And even animals,

00:04:56.940 --> 00:04:59.166
even animals were looking uncomfortable.

00:04:59.166 --> 00:05:05.380
And I think they were picking up on the emotions of the virus days,

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:11.820
and the emotions of the humans. And I think it's very interesting that animals,

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:12.880
I guess they haven't gotten this virus,

00:05:13.590 --> 00:05:19.789
so it must be strange for them. All the humans are nervous and edgy,

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:23.000
it feels like they could explode at any moment,

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:29.220
and then all the animals are just picking up on these feelings and they don't know what it is.

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:35.780
When the times get bad in this world, when there's a war, when there's tension between countries,

00:05:36.260 --> 00:05:39.440
when people are angry at being locked up,

00:05:39.820 --> 00:05:44.640
and then it breaks out. In this picture you can see rioting, 

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:50.880
pictures of rioting, people throwing things at the police, fires being set.

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:52.840
You know, in these times

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:56.720
when things are hard and we all feel frightened and

00:05:56.800 --> 00:06:01.720
we all feel nervous and we're all feel kind of depressed sometimes,

00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:06.640
then if you're nice to another person during this time,

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:10.460
you get a lot more karma added to your bank account.

00:06:10.780 --> 00:06:13.140
You get a lot more good seeds added to your bank account.

00:06:13.160 --> 00:06:15.360
That's what this section is talking about.

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:17.900
To keep your morality,

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:23.880
to be kind to other people, to share what you have when things are crazy,

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:26.900
then that's the sign of a real practitioner.

00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:30.180
That's the sign of a really good person.

00:06:30.340 --> 00:06:33.340
kalpa nga du lab shi yong dzok sungwa le--
BSKAL PA SNGA DUS BSLAB GZHI YONGS RDZOGS BSRUNG BA LAS

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:35.540
so they say

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:38.620
the world goes through these huge cycles,

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:42.080
and that's the subject of a book called the "Abhidharma Kosha."

00:06:42.779 --> 00:06:45.409
In the third chapter, they describe

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:50.400
amazing descriptions of the world, amazing descriptions of things,

00:06:51.460 --> 00:06:53.460
and strange things happen.

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:58.000
Humans come here from another planet,

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:01.100
and then they live here for millions and millions of years, and

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:04.880
then slowly things get worse and worse and worse.

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:07.330
People are more violent.

00:07:07.330 --> 00:07:09.728
People aren't so nice to each other.

00:07:09.728 --> 00:07:13.340
And then finally there's a nuclear war.

00:07:13.540 --> 00:07:16.300
The third chapter of the Abhidharma--

00:07:16.420 --> 00:07:21.760
which is about two and a half thousand years old, the text, the subject--

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:25.840
it talks about a fire which covers the whole earth. And,

00:07:26.440 --> 00:07:33.060
strangely, there are some people off on a vacation in the mountains--

00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:38.220
they went to climb a mountain somewhere--and they don't get burned up.

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:44.100
But they suddenly get this realization from the virus, and they think, "Wow, 

00:07:44.320 --> 00:07:50.760
maybe we've been hurting this planet. Maybe we've been hurting the other creatures on this planet.

00:07:51.480 --> 00:07:54.600
Maybe this whole nuclear war

00:07:54.680 --> 00:07:58.840
or this virus is a karma,

00:07:58.840 --> 00:08:04.020
because we have hurt the planet and we have hurt the other beings on this planet.

00:08:04.240 --> 00:08:08.240
We have taken advantage of them. We have treated them like slaves.

00:08:08.240 --> 00:08:12.400
We have killed themx whenever we wanted space for ourselves.

00:08:12.440 --> 00:08:13.780
And then maybe,

00:08:13.920 --> 00:08:18.540
a disease comes from those animals to us."

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:22.340
So there is a theme like that in the "Abhidharma Kosha."

00:08:22.340 --> 00:08:25.920
Then those people make a decision

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:28.020
to change their lifestyle.

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:30.820
They become more ecological.

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:34.360
They stop using so much of the world's resources.

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:37.680
They respect other life-forms'

00:08:37.800 --> 00:08:41.620
needs for space and prosperity.

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:46.340
And then slowly the karma changes of the planet.

00:08:46.340 --> 00:08:49.460
And so then it goes through these huge cycles.

00:08:49.620 --> 00:08:54.520
It goes through sixty cycles like that, and that's called a great kalpa (BSKAL PA),

00:08:54.620 --> 00:08:55.640
a great eon.

00:08:56.000 --> 00:09:01.820
So in the early part of the eons are good times.

00:09:01.900 --> 00:09:04.940
People who survived the holocaust,

00:09:05.160 --> 00:09:07.845
they are nice to each other, for a while.

00:09:07.845 --> 00:09:09.760
So those people

00:09:10.220 --> 00:09:12.220
discover the ten good deeds.

00:09:12.800 --> 00:09:18.000
It is traditionally said that they keep them very carefully,

00:09:18.360 --> 00:09:21.440
and they observe the ten good deeds very carefully.

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:29.680
Then time goes on and you reach what we call the bottom of the barrel times.

00:09:30.300 --> 00:09:34.800
We're actually very close to that bottom of the barrel right now. According to Abhidharma,

00:09:35.549 --> 00:09:40.789
we are close to the the worst times in the world right now.

00:09:42.509 --> 00:09:44.509
So if during this time,

00:09:45.060 --> 00:09:50.200
people are nice to each other and people keep their vows, okay.

00:09:50.620 --> 00:09:51.540
Here it says:

00:09:51.580 --> 00:09:54.780
deng sang lappa na chik rungpa pen yun che
(DENG SANG BSLAB PA SNA GCIG BSRUNG PA PHAN YON CHE)

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:58.780
So let's say you don't get to even the whole list of ten, 

00:09:59.279 --> 00:10:02.520
you don't get the list of ten good deeds.

00:10:02.520 --> 00:10:06.018
Someone teaches you the first one and then they have to go. 

00:10:06.569 --> 00:10:13.878
But if you just keep one of the ten good deeds in these hard times,

00:10:14.669 --> 00:10:19.362
then it's better than those people at the beginning of time, like Adam and Eve,

00:10:19.362 --> 00:10:21.829
who are already innocent and already nice.

00:10:22.940 --> 00:10:26.960
To keep... to be nice to other people

00:10:27.060 --> 00:10:28.320
when times are hard,

00:10:28.320 --> 00:10:32.357
when economy is bad, and when there's a lot of confusion, and

00:10:32.357 --> 00:10:34.740
when there's a lot of danger, illness,

00:10:35.120 --> 00:10:38.980
then to keep just one of the Buddhist rules

00:10:38.980 --> 00:10:47.300
is more powerful than keeping all of them for a long time, for millions of years.

00:10:47.680 --> 00:10:53.580
pen yun chewar sungpe sanggye mangpor kalpa chewar chupa le kyang de hlak la
(PHAN YON CHE BAR GSUNGS PAS SANGS RGYAS MANG POR BSKAL PA BYE BAR MCHOD PA LAS KYANG DE LHAG LA,)

00:10:53.580 --> 00:10:56.040
It's also better than making offerings to Buddhas for 

00:10:56.140 --> 00:10:59.800
millions of years, is to keep your patience

00:11:00.380 --> 00:11:03.297
when things are hard, when there's a lot of confusion,

00:11:03.297 --> 00:11:04.540
when people are divided,

00:11:05.399 --> 00:11:07.861
when there's a lot of danger with the virus.

00:11:07.861 --> 00:11:09.320
To be the calm one,

00:11:09.720 --> 00:11:11.455
to be the one who shares,

00:11:11.460 --> 00:11:16.400
to be the one who smiles when things are really crazy,

00:11:17.200 --> 00:11:20.300
then that's extremely powerful karma.

00:11:20.640 --> 00:11:22.740
That's what they're talking about.

00:11:22.840 --> 00:11:26.340
Why are we talking about being nice to other people? 

00:11:26.440 --> 00:11:28.900
We're talking about how to reach nirvana.

00:11:28.980 --> 00:11:30.220
Don't forget where we are in the text.

00:11:30.240 --> 00:11:32.620
We're talking about how to reach nirvana.

00:11:32.980 --> 00:11:35.480
tsultrim denpa sanggye jung dang tre
(TSUL KHRIMS LDAN PA SANGS RGYAS 'BYUNG DANG 'PHRAD)

00:11:36.020 --> 00:11:38.524
Then there's a famous sutra and

00:11:38.524 --> 00:11:44.800
it's called the "sutra where we honor the ethical way of life."

00:11:44.960 --> 00:11:46.940
Being a good person.

00:11:47.020 --> 00:11:51.000
The sutra called 'it's cool to be a good person.' 

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:55.040
There's a sutra like that, and it has a famous line in it.

00:11:55.080 --> 00:11:57.620
tsultrim denpa sanggye jung dang tre

00:11:57.860 --> 00:12:00.780
And there's two ways to read this line.

00:12:00.780 --> 00:12:02.180
You can say,

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:06.620
if a person is nice to other people,

00:12:06.920 --> 00:12:12.400
it's as if a Buddha has come to this planet and we have met the Buddha.

00:12:12.760 --> 00:12:18.280
If you're a person who shares what you have in these difficult times,

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:21.020
and if you're a person who is patient with people who are afraid

00:12:21.020 --> 00:12:25.920
or even violent in these difficult times,

00:12:26.120 --> 00:12:29.420
if you're the person who stays cool,

00:12:29.420 --> 00:12:31.840
then we can say the Buddha is walking on this planet.

00:12:31.843 --> 00:12:33.519
We have met the Buddha again.

00:12:34.070 --> 00:12:37.239
Then some people read this line as meaning

00:12:38.900 --> 00:12:41.340
when the Buddha comes back to this planet,

00:12:41.560 --> 00:12:43.649
you will have the seeds to meet them.

00:12:43.649 --> 00:12:46.700
And I think you can read it either way. 

00:12:46.760 --> 00:12:49.620
So, that's the famous line from that sutra. 

00:12:50.880 --> 00:12:55.140
The monks and nuns--wherever they live, whatever country they live in--

00:12:56.030 --> 00:12:57.500
twice a month,

00:12:57.500 --> 00:13:00.850
they're supposed to get together on the full moon and the new moon.

00:13:01.540 --> 00:13:05.120
They're supposed to sit down

00:13:05.320 --> 00:13:10.900
in a little group and everyone has... they have a green drink. 

00:13:11.140 --> 00:13:15.700
They're all sitting having a green drink,

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:19.753
and the leader says, "Anybody have anything they want to say?"

00:13:19.760 --> 00:13:23.620
And then somebody will say, "Yeah, I got something." "Well, what?"

00:13:24.340 --> 00:13:27.180
"Well, you know, actually I cheated on my taxes a little bit,

00:13:28.610 --> 00:13:34.209
last week. The taxes were due, you know, I was late. I wrote a letter, 

00:13:34.900 --> 00:13:39.040
I told the tax people my dog ate the paper." 

00:13:39.260 --> 00:13:43.360
Then they make confessions to each other and 

00:13:43.520 --> 00:13:45.980
it was a very sweet ancient requirement 

00:13:45.980 --> 00:13:47.530
of monks and nuns.

00:13:47.530 --> 00:13:50.889
I'm afraid nowadays, I'm sad to say,

00:13:52.360 --> 00:13:53.900
they just recite the words:

00:13:53.900 --> 00:14:00.740
chok chu na shukpay sanggye dang jangchub sempa tamche dang gendun tsunpa nam dak la
dong su sol, dak gelong ming di she gyi wa...
(PHYOGS BCU NA BZHUGS PA'I SANGS RGYAS DANG BYANG CHUB SEMS DPA' THAMS CAD DANG DGE 'DUN BTZUN PA RNAMS BDAG LA DGONGS SU GSOL, BDAG DGE SLONG MING 'DI ZHES BGYI BA)

00:14:00.780 --> 00:14:02.500
And then you just recite it and you go home.

00:14:02.720 --> 00:14:07.000
But the old system, which is very sweet for Dharma people... 

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:09.300
and if you're in a small Dharma group

00:14:09.460 --> 00:14:12.140
or you're in your lam rim Dharma group, 

00:14:12.340 --> 00:14:14.980
then tell each other when you make a mistake,

00:14:15.100 --> 00:14:17.780
it cleans it right away.

00:14:17.780 --> 00:14:20.700
Usually we work harder to hide our bad habits

00:14:21.200 --> 00:14:23.200
than we do to stop them.

00:14:24.200 --> 00:14:29.680
But if you just say, "Look, I have a bad habit. I want everybody to know, and I'm working on it."

00:14:29.980 --> 00:14:32.240
You know, I got a COVID tummy right now and

00:14:32.480 --> 00:14:35.980
last night I ate half a Häagen-Dazs ice cream.

00:14:35.980 --> 00:14:42.160
I'm telling the truth. Confess. Be honest. All right.

00:14:42.260 --> 00:14:44.720
So at the confession, nowadays,

00:14:45.040 --> 00:14:49.180
the leader of the confession--who's usually the abbot of the monastery--

00:14:50.060 --> 00:14:55.209
they will stand up and recite these holy sutras about keeping your vows.

00:14:55.880 --> 00:14:58.689
So here it says dawa che che na donpa-ang (ZLA BA PHYED PHYED NA 'DON PA'ANG)

00:14:59.300 --> 00:15:05.200
So when the leader of the confession group, which is called sojong (GSO SBYONG), 

00:15:05.420 --> 00:15:09.860
when they get up to recite the sutra do dunpa po (MDO 'DON PA PO),

00:15:09.900 --> 00:15:14.460
they are not... it's not like they're a kid in the monastery 

00:15:14.920 --> 00:15:21.640
who is assigned an examination topic where they had to recite the sutra. 

00:15:21.800 --> 00:15:26.140
Because that's a very common occurrence in the monastery 

00:15:26.240 --> 00:15:30.797
that the kids have to memorize a sutra that the teacher gave them.

00:15:30.800 --> 00:15:35.820
And they sit there shaking, and trying to recite the sutra by heart.

00:15:35.820 --> 00:15:43.220
Look, when the abbot of the whole monastery gets up and he recites these holy words,

00:15:43.340 --> 00:15:46.020
a person who treats other people nice,

00:15:46.040 --> 00:15:48.263
when you meet them, it's like meeting the Buddha.

00:15:48.263 --> 00:15:53.680
When he recites it, don't sit there and think he's some kid who's taking examination; he's not.

00:15:53.840 --> 00:15:58.000
And don't think also drang sok (GRANGS GSOG). 

00:15:58.220 --> 00:16:02.840
drang sok means when you recite a scripture over and over

00:16:03.080 --> 00:16:05.320
to get some kind of extra seeds.

00:16:05.460 --> 00:16:09.880
You know, like you take a rosary and you decide you're going to recite

00:16:09.980 --> 00:16:14.640
the Heart Sutra twenty-one times, which we do in the monastery--

00:16:14.980 --> 00:16:23.520
di ke dak gi tupay du chik na, chomdende gyalpoy kapna ja gu pungpoy ri la gelong gi gendun chenpo dang jangchup sempay gendun chenpo dang tap chik tu shuk te, dey tse chomdende zabmo nangwa shejaway chukyi namdrang kyi tingendzin la nyompar shuk so
('DI SKAD BDAG GIS THOS PA'I DUS GCIG NA, BCOM LDAN 'DAS RGYAL PO'I KHAB NA BYA RGOD PHUNG PO'I RI LA DGE SLONG GI DGE 'DUN CHEN PO DANG BYANG CHUG SEMS DPA'I DGE 'DUN CHEN PO DANG THABS CIG TU BZHUGS TE, DE'I TSE LDAN 'DAS ZAB MO SNANG BA ZHES BYA BA'I CHOS KYI RNAM GRANGS KYI TING NGE 'DZIN LA SNYOMS PAR ZHUGS SO,)

00:16:23.680 --> 00:16:28.940
So don't think the guy is trying to pile up on his rosary

00:16:29.060 --> 00:16:33.780
these Vinaya sutras, these sutras about how to be nice to people.

00:16:34.130 --> 00:16:37.719
And don't think he's taking an exam, because it's not--because he's already the abbot.

00:16:38.120 --> 00:16:44.580
By the way, those of you who are learning Tibetan--and we talked about it yesterday, me, and Seiji, and Tim--

00:16:45.540 --> 00:16:52.400
to take an exam in English, in American English, means you're the kid 

00:16:52.520 --> 00:16:54.060
and you are taking the exam from the teacher.

00:16:55.480 --> 00:16:57.560
But in Tibetan it's the opposite.

00:16:57.560 --> 00:17:03.120
The exam is extracted by the teacher, the teacher takes the exam from the student.

00:17:03.130 --> 00:17:05.560
Okay, so don't get confused by the Tibetan here.

00:17:06.520 --> 00:17:11.040
So that Abbot's not... he's not up there... it's not a game.

00:17:11.040 --> 00:17:13.440
He's not a kid. He's the abbot of the monastery.

00:17:14.080 --> 00:17:18.960
He's reciting those words drenpa so (DRAN PA GSO).

00:17:18.960 --> 00:17:21.480
drenpa so--he's trying to remind you 

00:17:21.820 --> 00:17:28.060
of how precious it is to be a nice person, especially when it's hard times.

00:17:28.060 --> 00:17:31.240
Like right now, in the times of the virus, 

00:17:31.400 --> 00:17:34.150
when people recite this line, 

00:17:34.700 --> 00:17:41.160
when a person is nice to other people, we can say that person is a Buddha walking on this planet.

00:17:41.160 --> 00:17:45.860
And when you hear them, when you see them share their toilet paper, 

00:17:45.860 --> 00:17:50.960
or you see them share their money when the economy gets bad,

00:17:50.960 --> 00:17:54.520
when you see them donating money... I have some friends right now, 

00:17:55.240 --> 00:18:00.520
this week they are making major donations. I'm like wow, you guys are...

00:18:01.200 --> 00:18:04.180
...it's cool. It's like I met a Buddha, you know. Everyone else is afraid.

00:18:04.660 --> 00:18:09.200
Everyone else is holding their money. And these people are like, "Do you need money? Do you need money?" 

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:14.180
Let's go like that, even in times of the virus.

00:18:15.600 --> 00:18:20.440
I enjoy going into John Brady's database--and thank you guys, all

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:23.980
you Gold Clubs and Jade Clubs and club clubs,

00:18:24.590 --> 00:18:27.370
around the world who are collecting donations,

00:18:28.060 --> 00:18:31.400
it's amazing! What you're doing is amazing.

00:18:31.660 --> 00:18:37.640
Even today we had a Yoga Studies Institute 

00:18:37.920 --> 00:18:43.600
and we were studying some deep, deep, deep ideas about the five envelopes, the five koṣas.

00:18:44.893 --> 00:18:49.000
We had John Brady's database. It's such a cool thing.

00:18:50.160 --> 00:18:53.740
John Brady to work on that for thirty-three years, that's unbelievable.

00:18:54.800 --> 00:18:59.160
So maybe that Buddha's been walking around for thirty-three years, okay?

00:18:59.300 --> 00:19:03.600
I wanted to recite to you the poetry from that sutra.

00:19:03.600 --> 00:19:05.180
I think it's beautiful. Okay, here we go...

00:19:06.040 --> 00:19:12.240
de chir tunpe tsultrim rab ngak she, tsultrim denpa sanggye jung dang tre,
(DE PHYIR STON PAS TSUL KHRIMS RAB BSNGAGS BSHAD,,TSUL KHRIMS LDAN PA SANGS RGYAS 'BYUNG DANG PHRAD,)

00:19:12.240 --> 00:19:34.580
tsultrim denpa gyen rnam kun gyi chok, tsultrim jorwa dri dang yukpa yin, tsultrim denpa gawa kun gyi ne, tsultrim denpa dungwa selway chu, tsultrim denpa jikten kun gyi tu, tsultrim dak gi drowa dampa nu, jitar drul dug lu chen nakpo yang, tsultrim chen la nu me shen chi mu, tsultrim denpay gelong u dang den, tsultrim denpa drak gyur dewa tob,
(,TSUL KHRIMS LDAN PA RGYAN RNAMS KUN GYI MCHOG
,TSUL KHRIMS 'BYOR BA DRI DANG BYUG PA YIN,
,TSUL KHRIMS LDAN PA DGA' BA KUN GYI GNAS,
,TSUL KHRIMS LDAN PA GDUNG BA SEL BA'I CHU,
,TSUL KHRIMS LDAN PA 'JIG RTEN KUN GYIS BSTOD,
,TSUL KHRIMS DAG GIS 'GRO BA DAM PA MNOS,
,JI LTAR SBRUL GDUG KLU CHEN NAG PO YANG,,TSUL KHRIMS CAN LA GNOD MED GZHAN CI SMOS,
,TSUL KHRIMS LDAN PA'I DGE SLONG 'OD DANG LDAN,
,TSUL KHRIMS LDAN PA GRAGS 'GYUR BDE BA THOB,)

00:19:35.140 --> 00:19:37.100
Let's just...

00:19:37.100 --> 00:19:41.240
Let's just read that... let's just translate that poetry.

00:19:41.520 --> 00:19:43.560
de chir tunpe tsultrim rab ngak she,
(DE PHYIR STON PAS TSUL KHRIMS RAB BSNGAGS BSHAD)

00:19:43.560 --> 00:19:45.320
The Buddha says

00:19:45.320 --> 00:19:48.579
being nice to people is cool, you are hip.

00:19:49.100 --> 00:19:51.459
You're like... what's the thing?

00:19:53.210 --> 00:20:00.550
What's the movie? They all run around in black clothes and they're all very hip? The Matrix. You're hip like the Matrix.

00:20:02.840 --> 00:20:04.289
Okay, the Buddha said that.

00:20:04.289 --> 00:20:06.800
tsultrim denpa sanggye jung dang tre,
(TSUL KHRIMS LDAN PA SANGS RGYAS 'BYUNG DANG PHRAD)

00:20:06.840 --> 00:20:11.221
If you're nice to other people, it's like I get to meet another Buddha.

00:20:11.221 --> 00:20:13.380
tsultrim denpa gyen rnam kun gyi chok,
(TSUL KHRIMS LDAN PA RGYAN RNAMS KUN GYI MCHOG)

00:20:13.570 --> 00:20:16.840
Don't worry about wearing a Cartier watch or 

00:20:17.600 --> 00:20:19.600
a Tiffany necklace, if you have...

00:20:20.060 --> 00:20:26.320
if you're treating other people nice, that's the most beautiful jewelry you can wear. 

00:20:27.710 --> 00:20:31.468
tsultrim jorwa dri dang yukpa yin, 
(TSUL KHRIMS 'BYOR BA DRI DANG BYUG PA YIN)

00:20:31.468 --> 00:20:35.640
When you are nice to other people,

00:20:35.840 --> 00:20:38.560
then you are putting on Chanel N°5.

00:20:38.560 --> 00:20:44.900
Then you really smell good. You know, they say that holy beings 

00:20:45.340 --> 00:20:50.040
can smell... a special smell when you're being nice to other people.

00:20:50.040 --> 00:20:53.920
It smells like great cologne or something.

00:20:54.100 --> 00:20:56.100
tsultrim denpa gawa kun gyi ne,
(TSUL KHRIMS LDAN PA DGA' BA KUN GYI GNAS)

00:20:56.720 --> 00:21:01.059
Everyone enjoys a person who is nice to other people.

00:21:01.940 --> 00:21:04.360
tsultrim denpa dungwa selway chu,
(TSUL KHRIMS LDAN PA GDUNG BA SEL BA'I CHU)

00:21:06.940 --> 00:21:13.080
Being nice to other people is like cold lemonade on a hot summer day. Okay, that's nice.

00:21:16.480 --> 00:21:18.560
tsultrim denpa jikten kun gyi tu,
TSUL KHRIMS LDAN PA 'JIG RTEN KUN GYIS BSTOD)

00:21:18.600 --> 00:21:24.220
Everyone talks about how cool people are when they are nice to other people.

00:21:24.950 --> 00:21:29.169
tsultrim dak gi drowa dampa nu,
(TSUL KHRIMS DAG GIS 'GRO BA DAM PA MNOS)

00:21:29.840 --> 00:21:31.138
drowa dampa nu--

00:21:31.138 --> 00:21:33.789
these are praised as the coolest people around.

00:21:34.400 --> 00:21:38.289
And there's a there's an error in the Kangyur (BKA' 'GYUR),

00:21:38.810 --> 00:21:40.580
so we fixed it.

00:21:40.580 --> 00:21:43.090
jitar drul dug lu chen nakpo yang,
(JI LTAR SBRUL GDUG KLU CHEN NAG PO YANG)

00:21:45.290 --> 00:21:47.470
Poisonous snakes, which we have a lot around here, and

00:21:49.010 --> 00:21:50.750
other kinds of problems,

00:21:50.750 --> 00:21:54.527
they can't touch a person who is being nice to other people.

00:21:54.527 --> 00:21:58.220
People keep asking me, "Oh Geshe-la, what's the karma

00:21:58.340 --> 00:22:00.720
that I shouldn't get the virus?" 

00:22:00.760 --> 00:22:05.840
Just be nice to other people, just serve other people, share what you have with other people.

00:22:05.840 --> 00:22:10.480
The viruses don't like those kind of people and they will avoid you.

00:22:11.420 --> 00:22:14.980
And then by the way, the sutra goes into saying,

00:22:16.370 --> 00:22:19.339
someone who's nice to other people is like a light in the world.

00:22:19.339 --> 00:22:21.519
We already talked about that part of the sutra.

00:22:23.000 --> 00:22:24.649
Okay.

00:22:24.649 --> 00:22:27.000
de le jungwa shin sam te
(DE LAS 'BYUNG BA BZHIN BSAM STE)

00:22:27.160 --> 00:22:28.460
so think about it...

00:22:28.580 --> 00:22:29.960
ke lang...

00:22:29.960 --> 00:22:32.860
ke langpay che tsam nam tsul shin sung
(KHAS BLANGS PA'I BCAS MTSAMS RNAMS TSUL BZHIN BSRUNG)

00:22:33.160 --> 00:22:36.760
Keep your commitments, keep the commitments you have.

00:22:39.200 --> 00:22:42.120
tenpay nyingpo ring du sel je shok
(BSTAN PA'I SNYING PO RING DU GSAL BYED SHOG,)

00:22:42.260 --> 00:22:46.580
then there's very... there's a lot of prayers 

00:22:47.260 --> 00:22:50.360
in Buddhism, there's a lot of lam rim prayers and

00:22:50.420 --> 00:22:53.940
they end this way:

00:22:54.500 --> 00:22:59.640
tenpay nyingpo ring du sel je shok--

00:22:59.640 --> 00:23:01.840
May I be the person

00:23:03.160 --> 00:23:06.060
who makes the teaching shine in the world.

00:23:06.300 --> 00:23:14.660
May I be the person who keeps these teachings shining like the sun in this world.

00:23:14.780 --> 00:23:19.480
May I be the person who keeps these teachings shining like the sun in this world. 

00:23:20.240 --> 00:23:26.160
And there's another version of that called lobsang gyelway tenpa gye gyur chik
(BLO BZANG RGYAL BA'I BSTAN PA RGYAS GYUR CIG)

00:23:26.940 --> 00:23:33.040
May the teachings of Tsongkapa, the Buddha Tsongkapa,

00:23:33.380 --> 00:23:36.700
may they spread in this world. It's a very, very famous prayer.

00:23:37.340 --> 00:23:42.580
May I be the person to spread these teachings in the world.

00:23:42.840 --> 00:23:45.580
May the teachings spread in the world.

00:23:45.880 --> 00:23:48.480
yang tor mar rang rang gi gyu la gyepa shik gu
(YANG THOG MAR RANG RANG GI RGYUD LA RGYAS PA ZHIG DGOS,)

00:23:48.940 --> 00:23:52.320
And we see here in the picture,

00:23:53.220 --> 00:23:55.280
fingers making a heart.

00:23:58.880 --> 00:24:02.020
And what the lama said in the lam rim,

00:24:02.860 --> 00:24:06.100
he said, "Come on! You guys, you sit here in the monastery and

00:24:07.620 --> 00:24:10.160
every day you recite these prayers and

00:24:10.640 --> 00:24:12.880
the last line of the prayer is always,

00:24:13.060 --> 00:24:17.700
'May I help the light of the Buddhas' teachings spread in the world

00:24:17.700 --> 00:24:21.320
May I take the Dharma 

00:24:21.320 --> 00:24:28.320
to every country in the world. May I be the supreme spreader of the Dharma 

00:24:28.320 --> 00:24:35.960
in all countries among all people. May I be the one who spreads it in the world.'"

00:24:35.960 --> 00:24:38.840
And then the lama said, "You know the best way to do that."

00:24:38.840 --> 00:24:40.180
And everybody's like, "What?"

00:24:40.280 --> 00:24:42.960
And he says, "Spread it here." [pointing to heart]

00:24:42.960 --> 00:24:44.276
It's very funny. 

00:24:44.276 --> 00:24:47.840
"Oh, you want to spread the Dharma in the whole world?" "Yeah."

00:24:48.280 --> 00:24:54.160
"Oh, you want to be the person who teaches everybody in the whole world the Dharma?" "Yeah."

00:24:54.160 --> 00:24:58.620
"Oh, you want to be this light that shines like the sun in the whole world?"

00:24:58.780 --> 00:25:03.460
"Yeah, yeah--that's me. I want to be that." "Okay. Well, how about you start here?

00:25:03.460 --> 00:25:05.919
And spread it like two inches here?" [at heart]

00:25:06.440 --> 00:25:08.180
Okay, and

00:25:08.180 --> 00:25:10.629
then we can say you're a Dharma spreader.

00:25:10.629 --> 00:25:15.480
Then we can say you're spreading the Dharma in the world. So spread it in your heart.

00:25:15.700 --> 00:25:18.600
Especially in these difficult times when things are so hard.

00:25:19.760 --> 00:25:24.099
Everyone's afraid. It's not just some people--everyone's afraid.

00:25:25.250 --> 00:25:27.250
This virus is amazing Buddhist practice,

00:25:28.070 --> 00:25:32.349
because it doesn't matter how much money you have, it doesn't matter where you live.

00:25:32.870 --> 00:25:37.000
It doesn't matter how powerful you are. It doesn't matter how many muscles you have.

00:25:38.510 --> 00:25:40.629
This virus is dangerous for everybody.

00:25:41.480 --> 00:25:48.460
So we can get afraid and we can lose our morality.

00:25:48.460 --> 00:25:52.900
We can start to cheat people or not share our things or

00:25:53.000 --> 00:25:55.000
steal toilet paper or

00:25:55.190 --> 00:25:58.450
we can start to throw things at people,

00:25:59.240 --> 00:26:01.420
rioting, breaking stores,

00:26:02.060 --> 00:26:04.060
you know?

00:26:04.700 --> 00:26:06.370
I just bought a small cafe.

00:26:06.370 --> 00:26:09.480
I worked really, really hard to fix it up.

00:26:09.700 --> 00:26:15.480
And I'm just watching on TV where people smashed these people's little stores.

00:26:16.010 --> 00:26:18.700
I'm like, "That's so dumb!" I mean you should

00:26:19.550 --> 00:26:21.550
smash... smash something

00:26:22.340 --> 00:26:27.900
rich people... these little guys tried so hard to build their little stores.

00:26:27.900 --> 00:26:30.600
And so... by the way, I'm not saying you should, 

00:26:30.600 --> 00:26:32.180
but I'm just saying

00:26:32.300 --> 00:26:34.040
resist this

00:26:34.040 --> 00:26:36.780
fear and resist this temptation

00:26:36.980 --> 00:26:41.620
to act crazy or to act in a way that hurts other people.

00:26:41.625 --> 00:26:43.450
A real Buddhist person

00:26:44.420 --> 00:26:46.420
during the time of the virus

00:26:47.050 --> 00:26:49.950
should become more peaceful, more moral,

00:26:50.500 --> 00:26:54.060
more kind, more generous than they were before.

00:26:54.320 --> 00:26:57.020
This is the time to do that. 

00:26:57.020 --> 00:26:58.680
Let's see in the next episode

00:26:58.690 --> 00:27:00.690
how we can do that.

00:27:00.850 --> 00:27:02.850
Thank you.

